A||||6||Mach10||Absent Air Conditioning.||||6||
Z||000000||Mach10||06-23-2001||02:08 PM||||There's no coolant in my AC. I know this. All that comes out of the purge valves is a sad little hiss. I don't really care, to be honest. Having said that, I know I am wasting energy by still having that AC belt turning the compressor pulley, engaged or not. Should I even waste the energy popping up the hood and taking a pair of bolt-cutters to the belt? I'll get the damn thing fixed someday. Just not anytime soon. ||||reg||6
Z||000001||terryk||06-23-2001||02:13 PM||||Since it is holding *some* pressure, leave it alone until you get it fixed. It will keep dirt out of the system which will double (or more) the cost of fixing it when you do.<P>The HP lost to spinning the pulley alone is nothing. Yes, it might take .1HP. If you are splitting the horsepower that close, you have the wrong car.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 06-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||06-23-2001||02:35 PM||||Remember that the "coolant" in your A/C system is a gas (when not engaged)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||06-23-2001||02:39 PM||||Actually, the hiss stopped after I had done it once. Never came back. I'd get it refilled (pretty sure it leaked out in the 7 years it sat. Most likely no huge leaks) but it needs the RS134 upgrade. I'm WAY too lazy. In fact, if it weren't for the fact that I'm so lazy, I'd punch you in the stomach for that "splitting horse[hairs]" comment  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>The engine will still load down when you hit the AC switch, and I was wondering if the ECM periodically turns on the AC pump. That would suck gas mileage... Nevermind then  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-23-2001||08:46 PM||||Leave the belt on to keep the pulley from rusting. Just spinning the pulley takes so little power I doubt anything but the most expencive engine dyno would be able to measure it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||06-23-2001||09:15 PM||||The load you detect when you hit the A/C button  is most likely the increased load to the alt. as the fan comes on when the A/C is activated||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||06-23-2001||09:23 PM||||Nifty, so If I'm drivin' in the city, I can use my now-defunct AC to force the fan on? Cool.<BR>Hey Ogre! This beats YOUR whole idea of wiring in a new switch! Just get people to puncture their AC hoses, and they have an instant fan!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
